Z||000003||FieroGTguy||07-07-2001||04:01 AM||||Exactly what I am looking for chester, thanks!<P>Did you use drop spindles with your coil overs to get the 2.5" drop?  If you were to get a chop top conversion, you would most certainly be the lowest Fiero.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Greg||||reg||10
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||07-07-2001||10:03 AM||||I will give it a try. I am posting a lot and ou can pick the ones you like the best. <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lucky1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lucky2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lucky3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lucky4.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lucky5.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lucky6.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lucky7.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||7
Z||000005||chester||07-07-2001||10:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroGTguy:<BR><B>Exactly what I am looking for chester, thanks!<P>Did you use drop spindles with your coil overs to get the 2.5" drop?  If you were to get a chop top conversion, you would most certainly be the lowest Fiero.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Greg</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well originally I got the front suspension used from a guy in Mississippi.  He had it on a 86 Northstar GT and upgraded to the Ryanes top of the line Slolum kit. Came with the tube control arms, coilovers and poly everything.  Also got his brake setup.  11" vented all around with functional emergency brake. Anyway, I installed the suspension in time to go to Carlise this year.  We got down there ok, went to the show and then trouble started.  I stopped on the way back at the local gas station to get noxzema for the burns (Awsome show! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).  Pulling out of the parking lot I tap the brake and hear this BAM!!! and the car tugs to the left nearly pulling the wheel out of my hand.  I'm like WTF??  So I drive it SLOWLY to the hotel.  I get out and ask my wife to watch the wheel as I apply the brake and watch for movement.  She tells me the brkae caliper was moving back and forth about 6 inches.  Wow!  So I jack up the car and find that the upper cotrol arm ripped off of the cross member! I mean the steel crossmember literally ripped around the weld!  Boy was I pissed!  Here it is Saturday at 7:00 in the evening. We were leaving the the AM.  Nice. So I call Eric Schneck who was out at his hotel (He know where the GOOD hotel was the bastard! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) and screamed HELP!  We drove around and finally came across a PETROL truck stop to do the tack welding for me.  Anyway, to make a long story short I found out that the suspension was modified by the previous owner and that the mod weaked the crossmember. And to make things worse I was on 495 on the way home and bottomed out HARD. Broke both front shocks.  There goes $400 in suspension parts. I had a set of drop spindles that I was going use but the setup had a 2" drop built in by the mods the prior owner did. So now I'm going back to the way the suspension was originally designed by RCC and am using my Street Dreams drop spindles to complete it right. I already have the replacemaent parts from RCC and sandblasted my old crossmember.  Its getting painted tomorrow (red) and I'm installing everything next Sunday (Saturday is our 2Nd annual swap meet at Kick Hill Farms, Lebonon Ct) and then get it aligned.  I have everything tack welded together so I can drive it for now. <P>Later.<P>Rob D.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Urchin||07-07-2001||11:23 AM||||I don't know if this is classified as "custom", but it is a '85 SE w/ the GT body on it.  A/R rims, 10"sub mounted under the dash (unfortunately no pics of that right now), 4cyl./auto<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_10.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front_9.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lowered_blackgtsig2a_2.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroGTguy||07-07-2001||08:07 PM||||Any mod will make the cut.  Paint, wheels, panels, engine, interior, etc...<P>I want to make a place that people can go to that want to modify their Fiero, but have questions about what can be done.<P>Even the Fiero experts don't know the full potential of mods people come up with.  I hope it inspires vendors to produce those mods in demand.<P>Keep them coming people, this will benefit everyone in the long run!  (Even if it will be a good post to open to see some cool Fieros!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Greg||||reg||1
